Employee Health and Wellbeing
Employee Health and Wellbeing
In today’s climate of greater health awareness, companies around the world are going beyond traditional attention to employee safety at work and considering employee health and wellbeing from a holistic standpoint. Such an approach considers engaging employees in monitoring and improving their overall health status as measured by core health parameters such as blood pressure, weight, cholesterol, smoking, physical activity and more. It addresses other health factors that affect overall wellbeing, including those that may, even indirectly, be accelerated through work, such as stress and anxiety. Such programs are generally recognized to improve productivity, reduce staff turnover and reduce healthcare expenses for both employers and employees.
