Materiality Assessment
Materiality Assessment
A materiality assessment is a foundational tool used by companies to identify, prioritize and strategically address relevant environmental, social and governance (ESG) topics that can have a significant impact on society or their business. Johnson & Johnson has been conducting such assessments, which we call Priority Topic Assessments (PTAs), since 2008, and we enhance our PTA methodology with each assessment. Typically, we have conducted the PTA every two to three years, but due to the continued world-shaping events of the COVID-19 pandemic and racial and social events of 2020, we conducted a PTA in 2020 and again in 2021.
